Spec: Time bounds

Purpose:
  Local-time bounds of days, weeks, years and month ranges as epoch-millisecond ranges, and the month test
    for month filters across years.

Owns:
  ./time_bounds.dart
  /test/domain/time_bounds_test.dart

References:
  /docs/specs/history/04-domain.md

Must:
  A week runs from Monday `00:00:00.000` to Sunday `23:59:59.999` local time.
  A day runs from `00:00:00.000` to `23:59:59.999` local time.
  A year runs from January 1 `00:00:00.000` to December 31 `23:59:59.999` of the given or current year.
  @monthRangeBounds runs from the first day of the start month to the last day of the end month within one
    year; a missing start means January, a missing end December.
  @monthOfYearInRange tests a timestamp's local month against an inclusive range; an inverted range matches
    no month and never wraps across the year end.

Scenario: Sunday belongs to the week that started on Monday
  Given now is a Sunday evening
  When the week bounds are computed
  Then the week starts on the preceding Monday at midnight
